So tell me about this magic of yours.

34
00:02:45,060 --> 00:02:45,900
Ceiling magic?

35
00:02:47,000 --> 00:02:48,920
I've never heard of that before.

36
00:02:49,320 --> 00:02:50,240
It must be rare.

37
00:02:50,440 --> 00:02:51,240
You're so lucky.

38
00:02:52,000 --> 00:02:53,340
How can we put it to use?

39
00:02:53,820 --> 00:02:55,420
Thinking about it is so exciting.

40
00:02:55,420 --> 00:02:58,260
Magical tools?

41
00:02:58,580 --> 00:02:59,000
That's right.

42
00:02:59,380 --> 00:03:03,420
With these, even someone born without any magic can use all kinds of spells.

43
00:03:04,020 --> 00:03:07,280
I think it'll be a good way to make our society more equal in the future.

44
00:03:07,820 --> 00:03:08,340
Equal?

45
00:03:08,760 --> 00:03:09,620
You're dreaming.

46
00:03:10,360 --> 00:03:13,700
It can be done, with the help of my magic items.

47
00:03:14,140 --> 00:03:17,120
I'm sure your ability will be a huge help in making them.

48
00:03:17,600 --> 00:03:18,060
I know.

49
00:03:18,060 --> 00:03:20,360
Can you seal magic into objects?

50
00:03:21,000 --> 00:03:22,200
Um, yes.

51
00:03:22,340 --> 00:03:23,200
Wow, really?

52
00:03:23,480 --> 00:03:24,280
That's perfect!

53
00:03:25,400 --> 00:03:29,100
And so, I helped the prince with his magical inventions.

54
00:03:29,100 --> 00:03:34,500
I'd never met anyone else like him in my whole life.

55
00:03:35,140 --> 00:03:40,380
There were some members of his family who resented him because of the progressive ideas that he'd champion.

56
00:03:41,040 --> 00:03:42,800
But he didn't let that bother him.

57
00:03:43,560 --> 00:03:47,600
He remained strong and honest, never compromising his beliefs.

58
00:03:47,600 --> 00:03:56,480
I didn't know it then, but the prince associated was a group that was different than humans.

59
00:03:57,240 --> 00:04:03,300
They were the elves, a race who was loved and blessed by mana, and who lived their lives in quiet peace.

60
00:04:04,900 --> 00:04:06,680
Wow, I can't believe it!

61
00:04:07,040 --> 00:04:10,240
Lit and his sword magic have been chosen by the four-leaf clover grimoire!

62
00:04:10,240 --> 00:04:12,460
What's so exciting, Mom?

63
00:04:12,800 --> 00:04:16,780
Well, you see, darling, only a select few were given a grimoire just like he got.

64
00:04:16,880 --> 00:04:18,780
It even comes with an extra helping of luck.

65
00:04:19,220 --> 00:04:19,740
Oh!

66
00:04:21,360 --> 00:04:23,420
Licked in his four-leaf grimoire!

67
00:04:23,840 --> 00:04:25,000
He's so cool!

68
00:04:28,560 --> 00:04:31,680
The three leaves of the clover each stand for something.

69
00:04:32,340 --> 00:04:35,880
One is integrity, one is hope, and one is love.

70
00:04:36,160 --> 00:04:38,080
Good luck dwells within the fourth leaf.

71
00:04:38,080 --> 00:04:41,020
And in the fifth leaf, there lives the devil.

72
00:04:41,940 --> 00:04:45,640
Back then, we all assumed that was nothing but an old saying.

73
00:04:46,320 --> 00:04:48,200
What do you think about all this?

74
00:04:48,760 --> 00:04:48,980
Hmm?

75
00:04:49,480 --> 00:04:53,680
You know, there's been a lot of talk about humans planning to attack us.

76
00:04:54,760 --> 00:04:56,140
I'm sure it's a rumor.

77
00:04:56,820 --> 00:04:59,100
It's still a possibility, though, isn't it?

78
00:04:59,440 --> 00:05:00,100
I mean, think.

79
00:05:00,460 --> 00:05:02,800
The human race is so wicked and mean-spirited,

80
00:05:02,900 --> 00:05:06,780
they slaughter helpless animals just for the sport of it without giving it a second thought.

81
00:05:08,080 --> 00:05:09,820
What's that thing?

82
00:05:09,820 --> 00:05:09,860
What's that thing?

83
00:05:17,680 --> 00:05:18,900
What's he doing?

84
00:05:19,660 --> 00:05:20,620
Sword magic.

85
00:05:21,100 --> 00:05:22,800
Now, origin flash.

86
00:05:23,960 --> 00:05:24,720
Light magic.

87
00:05:25,300 --> 00:05:26,160
Lamp of Avior.

88
00:05:26,160 --> 00:05:33,540
You're not hurt, are you?

89
00:05:33,920 --> 00:05:35,100
No, I'm fine.

90
00:05:35,860 --> 00:05:37,460
Thank you for saving me.

91
00:05:39,540 --> 00:05:41,560
Tatia, don't leave the castle like that.

92
00:05:41,940 --> 00:05:42,760
I'm sorry.

93
00:05:43,120 --> 00:05:47,540
Besides, a wind magic user like you isn't supposed to be getting herself caught in a mana tornado.

94
00:05:47,740 --> 00:05:48,400
What were you thinking?

95
00:05:48,400 --> 00:05:52,460
Thank you for helping my sister.

96
00:05:52,920 --> 00:05:53,400
It's no-

97
00:05:53,400 --> 00:06:07,280
Phenomenal magic talent.

98
00:06:08,060 --> 00:06:09,040
Similar ideals.

99
00:06:09,700 --> 00:06:11,540
The same four-leaf grimoires.

100
00:06:11,540 --> 00:06:16,780
For the first time, the prince had found a peer and licked the leader of the elves.

101
00:06:18,880 --> 00:06:20,640
Let's foster understanding.

102
00:06:21,520 --> 00:06:24,240
Your elvish mana really is a remarkable thing.

103
